# Persistence & infrastructure

## Persistence

- SQL Server + EF Core 10; configs under `Configurations/`, context under `Contexts/`.
- Add migrations in `Migrations/`; keep seed in `Seed/` (e.g. Identity seeder).
- Expose data through `IApplicationDbContext` for Application — do not leak concrete context into Domain.
- Prefer fluent entity configurations over attributes when matching existing style.

## Domain

- Entities/enums/value objects only; no MediatR, EF, or ASP.NET types (except Identity store abstractions already used).
- Put shared domain constants (e.g. `AppRoles`) in Domain/Common.

## Infrastructure

- Register Identity, JWT Bearer, and Persistence DI here (`DependencyInjection/`).
- Keep auth token issuance / identity adapters in Infrastructure; Application talks via contracts.

## Do not

- Query the DB from controllers.
- Add business workflows in Persistence interceptors unless the pattern already exists.
- Commit secrets or connection strings; use configuration / user secrets.
